Power BI Dashboard Explanation

The Power BI dashboard titled “Music Insights Dashboard” provides an interactive visualization of music analytics data, focusing on artists, albums, tracks, and popularity metrics. The dashboard consolidates information from multiple datasets and presents key performance indicators along with visual insights to help analyze trends in music production and track popularity. 

spotify project

Dashboard Objective

The objective of this dashboard is to provide insights into:

Total number of albums and artists available in the dataset

Track distribution across artists and albums

Popularity of tracks across different artists

Genre distribution and overall music trends

The dashboard enables users to explore relationships between artists, albums, tracks, and popularity scores through interactive visuals.

Key Metrics Displayed

The dashboard highlights several key performance indicators (KPIs):

Metric	Description
Total Albums	Total number of albums present in the dataset
Total Artists	Total number of unique artists
Total Tracks	Total number of tracks analyzed
Track Popularity	Popularity score representing track engagement
Average Track Duration	Average duration of songs in minutes

These metrics provide a high-level summary of the music dataset and help users quickly understand the scale of the data.

Dashboard Visualizations

The dashboard contains several visual components designed to highlight different aspects of the data.

Albums vs Artists Distribution (Pie Chart)

This visual compares the total number of albums and artists in the dataset.

Insights:

Albums represent approximately 67.87% of the dataset

Artists represent approximately 32.13%

This provides a quick overview of the dataset composition and shows that albums form the largest portion of the data. 

